<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="ea61bf12">The build should be properly tested prior to promoting to production.  Builds that is contains from unexecuted
code can mean the code is incorrect or a condition will not be met. In either case, it can mean a requirement was missed.
There are exceptions where unexecuted code is valid but should be verified.</attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="481aa090"></attribute>
<attribute name="usageGuidance" nodeId="964086c9"></attribute>
<attribute name="refinedDescription" nodeId="293d16bd">&lt;p&gt;
    The build should consist of an updated version of the application containing the latest changes and defect fixes
    which have the functionality expected from users based on the current requirements.  The build should
    contain all of the necessary support files for the application to execute correctly. 
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    The number of times a build is deployed ranges on the environment the build lives in. Builds in
    a development/testing environment will happen more frequently than in a production environment.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
